5.5).\n\n**Finding (real, confirmed):**\n- `app/src/components/PasswordGate.tsx:6` hardcodes `const CORRECT_PASSWORD = 'lightshow';` and compares user input against it client-side (`:30`).\n- The literal `lightshow` therefore ships in the built bundle: `dist/assets/index-*.js:19`.\n\n**Why it matters:** A client-side password is trivially bypassable (view source / read the JS) and the secret is world-readable in the deployed asset. Against a strict reading this fails Bootsie acceptance criteria AC3 (\"sensitive-pattern scan passes on the corpus AND deployable bundles\") and AC14 (\"no secret enters the deployable application\").\n\n**Scope note:** This is the *pre-existing Echo Springs app password gate*, not Bootsie-introduced. Bootsie's own corpus and bundle scanned clean (0 forbidden patterns, no run-book copy, no .env/.wrangler/D1/FastAPI, no XSS). The finding is escalated here to the parent rather than blocking the verification issue, because it predates and sits outside the Bootsie corpus/core surface.\n\n**Suggested remediation:** Move authentication to a server-side check (the Worker already enforces","status":"done","workMode":"standard","harnessKind":null,"priority":"high","assigneeAgentId":"2c6b1cc9-aad2-431b-93ea-e31f0612be65","assigneeUserId":null,"checkoutRunId":null,"executionRunId":null,"executionAgentNameKey":null,"executionLockedAt":null,"createdByAgentId":"dc2ca597-dd20-4a73-9fd3-8bef3da92ea9","createdByUserId":null,"responsibleUserId":null,"issueNumber":3771,"identifier":"JAC-3771","originKind":"manual","originId":null,"originRunId":null,"originFingerprint":"default","requestDepth":0,"billingCode":null,"assigneeAdapterOverrides":null,"executionPolicy":null,"executionState":null,"monitorNextCheckAt":null,"monitorWakeRequestedAt":null,"monitorLastTriggeredAt":null,"monitorAttemptCount":0,"monitorNotes":null,"monitorScheduledBy":null,"executionWorkspaceId":"d2da0ae7-91d2-46da-9e0f-79999bcde58e","executionWorkspacePreference":"reuse_existing","execut