        "name": "Echo Springs",
        "description": "## Purpose\nDigital guest guide and Bootsie concierge for Echo Springs Camp in Lyonsville, California. The project adapts the proven property-concierge pattern to Echo Springs as a fully isolated product and knowledge base.\n\n## Scope\n- Bootsie conversational concierge\n- Ten-chapter guest wiki as the RAG source\n- FastAPI backend and Cloudflare Pages guest surface\n- Self-managed property operations, with 911-first emergency guidance and no caretaker assumption\n\n## Canonical systems\n- Local code: `/Users/hermes/Projects/echo-springs-bootsie`\n- Guest site: `https://echo-springs.pages.dev`\n- Existing wiki: `https://echo-springs.jkre.is`\n- Work state: Paperclip\n\n## Current state\nEarly implementation exists, but production readiness remains incomplete. The local repository currently has no configured origin, so Paperclip uses a local-path workspace until a canonical remote is established.\n\n## Connections\n- [Sea Ranch AI](/projects/3edbceaa-842b-4cbd-8a2d-a06b9264db86) \u2014 sibling pattern source; no shared private data\n- [Agentic OS](/projects/f99704da-43b5-4cf7-89ef-13f59a348d90) \u2014 orchestration and deployment standards\n- [Onboarding](/projects/60bf492f-74ce-4084-83c9-d80c5f8bfaa9) \u2014 integration-readiness pattern\n- Accessible through the registered Paperclip MCP server; URLs are explicit cross-project pointers.\n\n**Stable project ID:** `97c2505c-53bb-4975-964f-0a5f6780b419`",
