    {
        "id": "b98b4689-2f85-41e8-87cf-580a324286c5",
        "companyId": "87c32b8e-f131-4df8-ad8e-963d01b458e7",
        "title": "AEGIS 2.2",
        "description": "# Fleet Workspace Configuration \u2014 Aegis\n\n**Created:** 2026-07-14 (JAC-3410)\n**Host:** Aegis (Mac Mini, 100.84.253.97, always-on)\n**Maintainer:** Coordinator (Paperclip dc2ca597)\n\n## Architectural Assessment: Are Separate Projects Getting in Our Way?\n\n**No.** The project separation is healthy and intentional. Each project serves a distinct domain:\n\n| Project | Purpose | Separation Justified? |\n|---|---|---|\n| Agentic OS (`~/Projects/agentic-os`) | Fleet dashboard, cron runtime, orchestration | Yes \u2014 Next.js app with its own build/deploy cycle |\n| Paperclip (`~/Projects/paperclip`) | Agent coordination server, 13-agent fleet | Yes \u2014 standalone Go server with its own API |\n| Sea Ranch AI (`~/Projects/sea-ranch-ai`) | Sally bot, Vista Del Mar guest knowledge | Yes \u2014 client brain, isolated by port :8081 |\n| Echo Springs (`~/Projects/echo-springs-bootsie`) | Property concierge, FastAPI on :8790 | Yes \u2014 separate service with wiki RAG |\n| Spine Federation (`~/Projects/spine-federation-aegis`) | Ringer waves, Beads pipeline, fleet spine | Yes \u2014 coordination infrastructure |\n| Prompt Kits (`~/Projects/prompt-kits`) | Pattern articles, skill source | Yes \u2014 content repository, not runtime |\n\n**What IS missing:** A single source of truth documenting how to access each environment, what ports are in use, and how Gemini access works. This document fills that gap.\n\n## Project Environments and Links\n\n### Active Services on Aegis\n\n| Service | Port | Process | Access |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Paperclip API | :3100 | paperclipai run | http://127.0.0.1:3100/api |\n| Bifrost (component federation) | :8078 | bifrost-http-0 v1.5.7 | http://127.0.0.1:8078 (HTML UI) |\n| ContextForge MCP Gateway | :8090 | mcpgateway (Python) | http://127.0.0.1:8090 (auth disabled) |\n| OB1 Agent Memory | :8787 | local brain (mxbai-embed-large, 1024 dim) | http://127.0.0.1:8787 |\n| Hindsight Daemon | :8888 | hindsight (bank: hermes) | http://127.0.0.1:8888 |\n| Honcho (self-hosted) | :8005 | Docker: honcho-hermes-aegis | http://127.0.0.1:8005 |\n| Ollama | :11434 | ollama serve | http://127.0.0.1:11434 |\n| Command Centre | :3012 | Next.js 16.2.1 | http://aegis.tailc2f398.ts.net:3012 |\n| Supabase Kong | :8000 | OrbStack container | (occupied) |\n| Supabase Pooler | :5432 | OrbStack container | (occupied) |\n\n### Models Available via Ollama (local)\n\n| Model | Size | Use Case |\n|---|---|---|\n| qwen3.6:latest | 23 GB | General reasoning |\n| qwen3-coder:30b | 18 GB | Coding (Coder agent) |\n| devstral-small-2:latest | 15 GB | Development |\n| gemma4:26b-a4b-it-qat | 15 GB | General tasks |\n| qwen3:8b | 5.2 GB | Lightweight tasks |\n| qwen2.5:7b | 4.7 GB | Honcho dialectic |\n| nomic-embed-text | 274 MB | Embeddings (768 dim) |\n| mxbai-embed-large | 669 MB | Embeddings (1024 dim) |\n\n### Gemini Access\n\n**Primary path (working):** agy CLI (Antigravity) at `/Users/hermes/homebrew/bin/agy`\n- Auth: OAuth 2.0 (user authentication, stored in macOS keychain as 'gemini')\n- Available models:\n  - Gemini 3.5 Flash (Low/Medium/High)\n  - Gemini 3.1 Pro (Low/High)\n  - Claude Sonnet 4.6 (Thinking)\n  - Claude Opus 4.6 (Thinking)\n  - GPT-OSS 120B (Medium)\n- Verified working: `agy --print \"What is 2+2?\" --model \"Gemini 3.5 Flash (Low)\" --dangerously-skip-permissions`\n- Usage: `agy --print \"prompt\" --model \"Gemini 3.5 Flash (Low)\" --dangerously-skip-permissions`\n\n**Hermes provider (CONFIGURED, awaiting API key):**\n- Hermes has built-in gemini provider (ID: gemini, name: Google AI Studio)\n- Provider added to ~/.hermes/profiles/aegis/config.yaml via hermes config set\n- Base URL: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta\n- Default model: gemini-3.5-flash; models: gemini-3.5-flash, gemini-3.1-pro, gemini-2.5-flash, gemini-2.5-pro\n- Env vars: GOOGLE_API_KEY or GEMINI_API_KEY in ~/.hermes/profiles/aegis/.env\n- **Status:** Provider config ready. Waiting for Jack to add GOOGLE_API_KEY=<key> to .env\n- Interaction 40d8a655 created (request_confirmation) for Jack to confirm key added\n- Keychain entry 'gemini' is agy's OAuth token (access_token), not an API key\n\n### Hermes Provider Configuration\n\nCurrent providers in ~/.hermes/profiles/aegis/config.yaml:\n- **ollama-launch**: http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1 (gemma4 models)\n- **mistral**: https://api.mistral.ai/v1 (mistral-large-latest)\n- **openai**: https://api.openai.com/v1 (gpt-5.1)\n- **gemini** (NEW): https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta (gemini-3.5-flash, gemini-3.1-pro, gemini-2.5-flash, gemini-2.5-pro) \u2014 awaiting GOOGLE_API_KEY in .env\n- **ollama-cloud** (default): https://www.ollama.com/v1 (glm-5.2)\n\nFallback chain: gemini \u2192 openai-codex \u2192 mistral \u2192 ollama-cloud (glm-5.2)\n\n### Paperclip Projects (5)\n\n| Project | ID | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Agentic OS | f99704da-43b5-4cf7-89ef-13f59a348d90 | Fleet dashboard, cron runtime, orchestration |\n| Sea Ranch AI | 3edbceaa-842b-4cbd-8a2d-a06b9264db86 | Sally bot, Vista Del Mar guest knowledge |\n| Echo Springs | 97c2505c-53bb-4975-964f-0a5f6780b419 | Property concierge |\n| Health | 24790c7e-0ab5-403c-89da-e13b0a460ea7 | Health tracking |\n| Onboarding | 60bf492f-74ce-4084-83c9-d80c5f8bfaa9 | Onboarding flows |\n\n### Bifrost Registered Components\n\nBifrost v1.5.7 at `~/.bifrost/config.json` registers these MCP clients:\n\n| Component | Connection | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| hermes | stdio | Hermes MCP server (local tools) |\n| notebooklm | stdio | NotebookLM integration |\n| nate_promptkit | stdio | Prompt kit tools |\n| cloudflare | stdio (mcp-remote) | Cloudflare MCP |\n| contextforge | stdio | ContextForge MCP gateway |\n| agentic_os_surfaces | stdio | Agentic OS dashboard surfaces |\n\n### ContextForge\n\n**Local gateway:** mcpgateway on :8090\n- Binary: `/Users/hermes/ai-dev/contextforge-gateway/.venv/bin/mcpgateway`\n- Start script: `/Users/hermes/ai-dev/contextforge-gateway/start-mcpgateway.sh`\n- Auth: disabled (AUTH_REQUIRED=false, MCP_REQUIRE_AUTH=false)\n- Database: SQLite at `data/mcp.db`\n- Token agekey: `~/.config/contextforge/contextforge-token-agekey.txt`\n- **SaaS status:** Not reachable (no endpoint configured)\n\n### Herdr Workspaces (live)\n\n| # | Label | Working Dir | Panes | Tabs |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | ~ | (home) | 1 | 1 |\n| 2 | Aegis Agentic OS | ~/Projects/agentic-os | 3 | 3 |\n| 3 | agentic-os | ~/Projects/agentic-os | 1 | 1 |\n| 4 | Aegis Notes | ~/=notes | 6 | 6 |\n| 5 | Aegis Prompt Kits | ~/Projects/prompt-kits | 3 | 3 |\n\n### Herdr-Plus Project Configs\n\n7 project configs at `~/.config/herdr/plugins/config/cloudmanic.herdr-plus/projects/`:\n\n| Config | Name | Group | Working Dir |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| agentic-os.toml | Aegis Agentic OS | Fleet | ~/Projects/agentic-os |\n| echo-springs-bootsie.toml | Aegis Echo Springs | Property | ~/Projects/echo-springs-bootsie |\n| fleet-health.toml | Fleet Health Dashboard | Fleet | ~/.hermes/profiles/family |\n| notes.toml | Aegis Notes | Fleet | ~/=notes |\n| paperclip.toml | Aegis Paperclip | Fleet | ~/Projects/paperclip |\n| prompt-kits.toml | Aegis Prompt Kits | Fleet | ~/Projects/prompt-kits |\n| sea-ranch-ai.toml | Aegis Sea Ranch AI | Property | ~/Projects/sea-ranch-ai |\n| spine-federation.toml | Aegis Spine Federation | Fleet | ~/Projects/spine-federation-aegis |\n\n### Herdr-Plus Quick Actions\n\n6 quick actions at `~/.config/herdr/plugins/config/cloudmanic.herdr-plus/quick-actions/`:\n\n| Config | Name |\n|---|---|\n| beads-status.toml | Beads Status |\n| check-ob1-health.toml | Check OB1 Health |\n| coordination-bus.toml | Coordination Bus |\n| paperclip-agents.toml | Paperclip Agents |\n| paperclip-board.toml | Paperclip Board |\n| ringer-model-scoreboard.toml | Ringer Model Scoreboard |\n\n### Paperclip Fleet Roster (13 agents)\n\n| Agent | ID | Adapter | Role |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Coordinator | dc2ca597 | hermes_local | Task routing, delegation |\n| Coder | 181f381b | opencode_local | Heavy coding (qwen3-coder:30b) |\n| Fable | f1ef5e14 | hermes_local | Front-end, design |\n| Researcher | 785cac12 | hermes_local | Web research |\n| Operator | a5d0eb09 | hermes_local | General ops |\n| Scout | c093061e | hermes_local | Lightweight tasks |\n| Bright | 8b6ea7f8 | hermes_local | Fleet planning |\n| Analyst-Opus | 6f075642 | hermes_local | Deep reasoning |\n| Analyst-Sonnet | e6ec3f05 | hermes_local | Reasoning fallback |\n| Analyst-Gemini | e8958dac | hermes_local | Non-Claude reasoning |\n| Watchdog | 3fad92dc | hermes_local | Fleet health |\n| Task Rabbit | d4bcfdbe | hermes_local | Overflow handler |\n| Wings | 80284e06 | hermes_local | Hermes edition coordinator |\n\n## Future Path: Config-Update Skill / PrintingPress CLI\n\n### Config-Update Skill Path\n\nA Hermes skill could automate fleet configuration updates:\n- Read current state from Bifrost, Herdr, Paperclip, Hermes config\n- Validate changes before applying (dry-run mode)\n- Propagate config changes across fleet surfaces\n- Atomic updates with rollback\n\n### PrintingPress CLI\n\n- PrintingPress Library discovery skill installed for Hermes (hermes skills install mvanhorn/printing-press-library/skills/printing-press-library -y)\n- PrintingPress binary installed: cli-printing-press 4.28.0 (via go install with Go 1.26.5)\n- Go upgraded to 1.26.5 via Homebrew (was 1.26.4)\n- Binary location: ~/go/bin/cli-printing-press (symlinked to ~/homebrew/bin/cli-printing-press)\n- PrintingPress skills installed for Claude Code (printing-press, printing-press-reprint, printing-press-polish, printing-press-score, etc.)\n- PrintingPress has 332 CLIs across 20 categories at printingpress.dev/library\n- pp at /usr/bin/pp is Perl PAR Packager, NOT PrintingPress\n- Candidate: generate a pp-fleet-config CLI from the workspace config API\n- Reference: docs/architecture/printing-press-agentic-os-candidates.md in worktree\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Blocked on Jack:** Add GOOGLE_API_KEY to ~/.hermes/profiles/aegis/.env \u2192 Gemini becomes active. Interaction 40d8a655 pending confirmation.\n2. **Complete:** PrintingPress installed (binary + skills). Go 1.26.5 downloaded.\n3. **Complete:** Hermes Gemini provider configured (providers.gemini in config.yaml).\n4. **Short-term:** Create fleet-config-sync Hermes skill (JAC-3412, blocked on API key)\n5. **Medium-term:** Generate pp-fleet-config CLI via PrintingPress for automated workspace provisioning\n6. **Long-term:** Use PrintingPress to generate CLIs for other fleet surfaces (Paperclip, Bifrost, Herdr)",
